height=\"60\" x=\"853\" y=\"840.5\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4056.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(5057,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(5557,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p>We need to find gravitational potential energy of a unit mass placed at the point P.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l31joqgd/480f9305-5b33-42d9-85e1-292436ec3e7b/0a0db0e0-d124-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31joqge.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l31joqgd/480f9305-5b33-42d9-85e1-292436ec3e7b/0a0db0e0-d124-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31joqge.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Gravitation Question 12 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l31joqgd/480f9305-5b33-42d9-85e1-292436ec3e7b/0a0db0e0-d124-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31joqge.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l31joqgd/480f9305-5b33-42d9-85e1-292436ec3e7b/0a0db0e0-d124-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31joqge.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l31joqgd/480f9305-5b33-42d9-85e1-292436ec3e7b/0a0db0e0-d124-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31joqge.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l31joqgd/480f9305-5b33-42d9-85e1-292436ec3e7b/0a0db0e0-d124-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31joqge.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l31joqgd/480f9305-5b33-42d9-85e1-292436ec3e7b/0a0db0e0-d124-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31joqge.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l31joqgd/480f9305-5b33-42d9-85e1-292436ec3e7b/0a0db0e0-d124-11ec-b5bf-9d106fd05fc4/file-1l31joqge.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>The surface mass density of the annular disc is</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"37.161ex\" height=\"2.452ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.9 16425.2 1083.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(849.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1905.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D440\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D440\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2956.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3456.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(3845.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(4845.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(5418.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D445\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D445\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(792,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(6836.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TE